# CSAF artifacts are hashed (.sha512) and signed (.asc) byte-for-byte, so git
# must not rewrite their line endings.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true and no rule here, git stored LF while the hashes and
# signatures were produced against the CRLF working tree. Every consumer
# fetching the raw files then saw a hash mismatch and a BAD signature, because
# raw.githubusercontent.com serves the stored blob, not the working tree.
#
# "-text" disables all end-of-line conversion, so what is committed and served
# is exactly what was hashed and signed. Diffs still work ("binary" would also
# disable those).
csaf/** -text
